{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>The sun</b> — alone, and the moon participates. And because the sun is beneath the earth at night, it has no power; were it not for the light of the moon and the stars, no living thing or plant would survive. And with all these, He mentioned: \"for His steadfast love endures forever\" — that He does so continually. Now He returns to mention that we are obligated to give thanks to HaShem for the signs He performed on behalf of His people, and He began with the smiting, after having mentioned the smiting of Egypt — He specified the firstborn, and this is great steadfast love toward Israel, to take vengeance against their enemies."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 136, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:41:53.951151985Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}